live-draw: conditional rendering (NV4097 SET_RENDER_ENABLE mode 2) through D3D12 occlusion queries and predication.

KZ3's level frame tests one proxy per light / shadow cascade (CLEAR_REPORT_VALUE 1, one colour-masked draw,
GET_REPORT type 1 at offset X) and draws the shadow map and the light with SET_RENDER_ENABLE (2 << 24) | X: the RSX
skips them when the ZPASS count is 0 (395 draws per level frame in the RPCS3 captures). Before, all of them ran.

1. rsx_dispatch: a new sink callback `report` gets CLEAR_REPORT_VALUE (0x17C8), SET_ZPASS_PIXEL_COUNT_ENABLE
   (0x17CC) and GET_REPORT (0x1800) in FIFO order.
2. live-draw: the ZPASS counter becomes D3D12 occlusion queries (heap of 8192). A segment (one query) opens at the
   first draw while ZPASS counting is on and closes at CLEAR_REPORT_VALUE, GET_REPORT, ZPASS off or a command-list
   flush. GET_REPORT X marks slot X: NEVER (no draw since the clear, count 0: skip on the CPU), PENDING (one
   segment: resolved into a 1024-slot predication buffer at the first draw that needs it) or ALWAYS (several
   segments or another report type: draw unconditionally, the conservative answer). Predicated draws run under
   SetPredication(buffer, slot, EQUAL_ZERO), cleared right after the draw, so host passes are never predicated.
3. The CPU-visible report value in guest memory is unchanged (cellGcmSys still writes "visible").
4. LD_COND_RENDER=0 turns it off. Log: "[cond-render] on", and every 256 flips (cellGcmSys.c gcm_flip_request) the counters (predicated, skipped,
   unconditional, resolves, reports, segments); rsx_live_draw_debug_cond_render_stats() for tests.

Host test tools/smoke/test_cond_render.c (PASS; LD_COND_RENDER=0 FAIL).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): context only, upstream immediate_vertex sink member added next to ours (PR292), both kept.

